#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "Test message from %(site)s"
msgstr "Message de test de %(site)s"

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "This is a test message from %(site)s.\\n\\nIf you are reading it, this instance can send mail: registration confirmations, section messages and reminders will all arrive."
msgstr "Ceci est un message de test de %(site)s.\\n\\nSi vous le lisez, cette instance sait envoyer du courrier : confirmations d'inscription, messages de section et rappels arriveront tous."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "The mail backend reported that it sent nothing."
msgstr "Le service d'envoi indique n'avoir rien envoyé."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "Check EMAIL_URL (or MAIL_SEND_MODE) and DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL in this instance's environment."
msgstr "Vérifiez EMAIL_URL (ou MAIL_SEND_MODE) et DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL dans l'environnement de cette instance."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "Send and finish"
msgstr "Envoyer et terminer"

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "Done"
msgstr "Terminé"

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "The code is in the web container's log, printed when the instance started. `docker compose logs web | grep -i \\\"setup code\\\"` shows it again, and `manage.py setup_code` prints it on demand."
msgstr "Le code se trouve dans le journal du conteneur web, affiché au démarrage de l'instance. `docker compose logs web | grep -i \\\"setup code\\\"` le réaffiche, et `manage.py setup_code` l'imprime à la demande."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "That is not this instance's setup code."
msgstr "Ce n'est pas le code d'installation de cette instance."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "The password for this account. Make it a long one."
msgstr "Le mot de passe de ce compte. Choisissez-le long."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "An account with this address already exists. Use a different address, or sign in with that one."
msgstr "Un compte existe déjà avec cette adresse. Utilisez une autre adresse, ou connectez-vous avec celle-ci."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "A unit needs at least one branch."
msgstr "Une unité a besoin d'au moins une branche."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "Branch %(number)s"
msgstr "Branche %(number)s"

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "Branch %(number)s needs a name."
msgstr "La branche %(number)s a besoin d'un nom."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "%(branch)s: the youngest age is above the oldest."
msgstr "%(branch)s : l'âge du plus jeune dépasse celui du plus âgé."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "%(branch)s needs at least one section."
msgstr "%(branch)s a besoin d'au moins une section."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "%(branch)s: every section needs a name."
msgstr "%(branch)s : chaque section a besoin d'un nom."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "Too many wrong codes from this address. Try again in %(minutes)s minutes."
msgstr "Trop de codes erronés depuis cette adresse. Réessayez dans %(minutes)s minutes."

#: members/wizard (hand-added; see docs/dev/CONTRACT.md)
msgid "Stable identifier from a branch preset, used to recognise this branch again when the preset is applied a second time."
msgstr "Identifiant stable issu d'un préréglage de branches, qui permet de reconnaître cette branche quand le préréglage est appliqué une seconde fois."
